{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidualAmplification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidualAmplification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.r_amplification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.r_amplification","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingResidualAmplification.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**`r = g₂ − 1` inherits the same amplification** (subtracting the constant `1` does not change the\nsensitivity): the residual moves by `δ·E/(Ep·hsq)` under a relative binding perturbation `δ`. So\nresolving `r` to absolute precision `η` requires the binding to relative precision\n`η·Ep·hsq/E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2_amplification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2_amplification","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingResidualAmplification.lean#L53-L61","doc":"**The amplification identity.** A *relative* perturbation `δ` of the measured binding\n(`E ↦ E·(1+δ)`) shifts `g₂` by exactly `δ · E / (Ep · hsq)`. The coefficient\n`E/(Ep·hsq)` is the amplification factor (`≈ 23.9` at `q₀`): the `1/h²` magnifies the binding's\nrelative error into `g₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2_affine","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingResidualAmplification.lean#L46-L51","doc":"**`g₂` is affine in the binding** `E`: `g₂ = E · (1/(Ep·hsq)) − 1/hsq`. The slope is\n`1/(Ep·hsq)`; there is no higher-order dependence on `E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BindingResidual.g2","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BindingResidualAmplification.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The bar-even coefficient as a function of the (measured) binding `E`, given the pure-theory\nframe energy `Ep = E⁺` and unit `h²` (`hsq`). Definition of `#4158`'s `g₂`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}